ad_creative_bodies:
Javier Palomarez, President and CEO of ‪@ushispanicbusiness‬, addresses the escalating fentanyl crisis and its impact across the nation. Palomarez emphasizes the need to listen to governors, border patrol, and immigration officials to develop an informed strategy. He calls for bipartisan cooperation, urging leaders to move beyond politics and fear mongering to tackle this critical issue for the good of all Americans. 

Watch to understand why this crisis demands immediate and united action from our elected officials.

@ntdnews #fentanylcrisis #ushbc

Loudoun County Public Schools Superintendent Aaron Spence spent over a month traveling to various conferences while students were overdosing on fentanyl. 
•
@LCPSofficials
@LoudounSupe

Please SHARE: 

I’ve got a record to stand on…

📝 Proud, involved community member, family man, small business owner, 6th generation Rockwall County resident. Member and volunteer of Lakepointe Church. 

🔔 During the most recent 88th Legislative Session, one of the most conservative sessions in Texas history, I made it a priority to support important measures that would ensure the growth and prosperity of the Lone Star State, including legislation:

🏡 Reducing the burden of property taxes on business and homeowners;

🔎 Fought AGAINST high density development and the McLendon-Chisholm crooked MUD development. 

🏥 Banning gender modification treatments for minors;

🚧 Advancing additional security measures to secure the border;

❌ Restricting children’s access to sexually explicit performances and materials;

🖥️ Ensuring all Texans, especially children, are protected online;

💊 Tackling the growing fentanyl crisis;
Cracking down on drug cartels and trafficking; and

💰 Implementing a balanced, fiscally responsible state budget for the next two years.

From HD-33 and For HD-33. For Texas.

